    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1782" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀέσκω</span></b> , Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.436
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>EM</u>
			20.11
		</span></i>: impf.
		
			Med.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀέσκοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			: aor. 1
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄεσα, ἀέσαμεν</span>, 
				contr.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσαμεν, ἄεσαν</span>, inf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀέσαι</span>:—<i>sleep</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.342
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.151
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				490
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.884
			</span></i>. (Etym. dub., but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύκτα ἀ.</span>
			has been expl. as <i>pass, spend</i> the night, cf. Skt.
				<i>vásati.</i>) [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ</span> metri gr. or by contraction, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ</span> otherwise.]</div>
